  "result": "107882.fm (https://www.merckmillipore.com/INTERSHOP/web/WFS/Merck-CH-Site/fr_FR/-/CHF/ShowDocument-Pronet?id=18328)\nciteturn42view0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: application/pdf; Number of pages: 1; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://www.merckmillipore.com/INTERSHOP/web/WFS/Merck-CH-Site/fr_FR/-/CHF/ShowDocument-Pronet?id=18328\",\"lineno\":10}); Total lines: 45\nL0@P0: 1 Merck Microbiology Manual 12th Edition\nL1@P0: Standard I Nutrient Broth\nL2@P0: These culture media are suitable for the cultivation of fastidious bacteria; after addition of blood, ascites fluid or serum\nL3@P0: they can also be used to cultivate streptococci, pneumococci and erysipelas organisms etc. They are employed for the\nL4@P0: enumeration, isolation and enrichment of bacteria and also as high-grade bases for preparing special culture media.\nL5@P0: In Vitro Diagnostic Medical Device –\nL6@P0: For professional use only\nL7@P0: Version 17-10-2008\nL8@P0: Merck KGaA, 64271 Darmstadt\nL9@P0: See also General Instruction for Use\nL10@P0: „How to use Dehydrated Culture Media“\nL11@P0: For MSDS, warnings and precautions see our website:\nL12@P0: www.merck-chemicals.com\nL13@P0: Principle\nL14@P0: Microbiological method.\nL15@P0: Typical Composition (g/litre)\nL16@P0: Peptones 15.0; yeast extract 3.0; sodium chloride 6.0; D(+)glu\u0002cose 1.0.\nL17@P0: Preparation\nL18@P0: Suspend 25 g Standard I Nutrient Broth/litre, autoclave (15 min\nL19@P0: at 121 °C).\nL20@P0: pH: 7.5 ± 0.2 at 25 °C.\nL21@P0: The prepared media are clear and yellowish-brown.\nL22@P0: Storage\nL23@P0: Usable up to the expiry date when stored dry and tightly closed\nL24@P0: at +15 to +25 °C. Protect from light.\nL25@P0: After first opening of the bottle the content can be used up to the\nL26@P0: expiry date when stored dry and tightly closed at +15 to +25 °C.\nL27@P0: Specimen\nL28@P0: e.g. Blood .\nL29@P0: Clinical specimen collection, handling and processing, see gen\u0002eral instructions of use.\nL30@P0: Experimental Procedure and Evaluation\nL31@P0: Depend on the purpose for which the media are used.\nL32@P0: Incubation: 24 h at 35 °C aerobically.\nL33@P0: Ordering Information\nL34@P0: Quality control\nL35@P0: Product Ordering No. Pack size\nL36@P0: Standard I Nutrient Broth 1.07882.0500 500 g\nL37@P0: Test strains Growth\nL38@P0: Staphylococcus aureus ATCC 25923 good / very good\nL39@P0: Streptococcus pyogenes ATCC 12344 good / very good\nL40@P0: Streptococcus pneumoniae ATCC 6301 good / very good\nL41@P0: Listeria monocytogenes ATCC 19118 good / very good\nL42@P0: Erysipelothrix rhusiopathiae ATCC 19414 fair / good\nL43@P0: Escherichia coli ATCC 25922 good / very good\nL44@P0: Shigella flexneri ATCC 12022 good / very good\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nBD DIFCO™ Heart Infusion Broth 500g - 238400 | BD (https://www.bd.com/en-us/products-and-solutions/products/product-page.238400)\nciteturn42view1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://www.bd.com/en-us/products-and-solutions/products/product-page.238400\",\"lineno\":230}); Total lines: 510\nL84:       * 【31†BD Learning Academy】\nL85:       * 【32†Interventional Education and Research】\nL86:   * 【33†Support】\nL87:     * 【2†Customer Portals】\nL88:       * 【34†BD Learning Academy†academy.bd.com】\nL89:       * 【35†Customer Care Portal Guides and FAQ’s】\nL90:       * 【36†Medication Management Customer Login†my.bd.com】\nL91:   * 【37†About BD】\nL92:     * 【38†Our Company】\nL93:       * 【39†About BD】\nL94:       * 【40†Segments】\nL95:       * 【41†Leadership】\nL96:       * 【42†Board of Directors】\nL97:       * 【43†Ethics and Compliance】\nL98:     * 【44†Communities】\nL99:       * 【45†Georgia】\nL100:       * 【46†Nebraska】\nL101:       * 【47†New Jersey】\nL102:       * 【48†South Carolina】\nL103:       * 【49†Utah】\nL104:     * 【50†Cybersecurity at BD】\nL105:       * 【50†About Us】\nL106:       * 【51†Trust Center